## Fee Clarification: Exit Load
### Reusable Support Snippet

  • An exit load is a charge levied by the mutual fund when units are redeemed before the scheme‑specified holding period expires.
  • It is a redemption charge imposed by the fund house, not a brokerage fee charged by brokers or platforms.
  • The load is applied only on early redemptions; holdings that meet or exceed the prescribed period are not subject to the charge.
  • The applicable percentage is disclosed in the scheme's offer document and is consistent across all distribution channels.
  • In a SIP, each installment has its own holding period, so redeeming any installment before its individual tenure may attract an exit load.
  • GST at the prevailing rate is charged on the exit load amount, and the total deduction includes both the load and the GST.

**Official Sources:**
  - https://www.sebi.gov.in/legal/circulars/jun-2009/exit-load-mutual-funds_3555.html
  - https://www.amfiindia.com/investor-corner/knowledge-center/exit-load

